  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Suppose A is a group which belongs to a variety V of groups, and which is\nembeddable in the full symmetric group S on an infinite set. Must the coproduct in\nV of two copies of A also be embeddable in S? (N. G. de Bruijn proved that this is\ntrue if V is the variety of all groups.)                            G. M. Bergman",
